	<Description>The intensity of a weak pulsing source is detected with a photomultiplier, which is probabilistic and dependent on the intensity. In the focus, the intensity is high during a pulse and this leads to a high probability of detection events for Photomultiplier 2. The other one (Photomultiplier 1) is placed in an area with relatively low intensity and hardly triggers.</Description>
